29_by_John_Bowles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Puzzle (1756): etching by John Bowles. In one variation on a recurrent joke, four antiquaries struggle to decipher what seems to be an ancient inscription, but which is in fact a crude memorial in English to Claud Coster, tripe-seller, and his wife. The print is ironically dedicated to \"the Penetrating Genius's of Oxford, Cambridge, Eaton, Westminster, and the Learned Society of Antiquarians\".","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Puzzle_(Gravestone_to_Claud_Coster_and_Jane_Coster_with_4_unknown_antiquaries)_by_John_Bowles.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Chardin%2C_la_scimmia_antiquaria%2C_1726_ca._02.JPG/500px-Chardin%2C_la_scimmia_antiquaria%2C_1726_ca._02.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Chardin%2C_la_scimmia_antiquaria%2C_1726_ca._02.JPG/1280px-Chardin%2C_la_scimmia_antiquaria%2C_1726_ca._02.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Chardin%2C_la_scimmia_antiquaria%2C_1726_ca._02.JPG/500px-Chardin%2C_la_scimmia_antiquaria%2C_1726_ca._02.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Le Singe Antiquaire (c. 1726) by Jean-Siméon Chardin","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChardin%2C_la_scimmia_antiquaria%2C_1726_ca._02.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Rowlandson_Death_%26_Antiquaries.jpg/250px-Rowlandson_Death_%26_Antiquaries.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/73/Rowlandson_Death_%26_Antiquaries.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/t